{"id": 48, "ts": 1780432174.1704829, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I see that both Sarah and James have leaned toward Candidate\u202fC, largely because of his quick decision\u2011making and strong attention to detail. However, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the safer overall fit for a long\u2011distance pilot.\u202fB\u2019s very conscientious nature and proven ability to handle stress well directly address our top criteria of operational reliability and stress resilience\u2014both non\u2011negotiable for international routes. Moreover, his skill in assessing weather conditions is a critical technical competence for long\u2011haul flights, and his excellent computer skills support the complex systems management required in modern cockpits. While I acknowledge the concerns about his pretentiousness and occasional tone issues, these are comparatively minor communication flaws that can be mitigated through crew\u2011resource\u2011training, especially given his strong reliability and calmness under pressure. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC\u2019s egocentric attitude, reluctance to pursue further education, and difficulty communicating ideas raise serious doubts about his adaptability, crew cooperation, and long\u2011term development\u2014areas where we cannot afford compromise. Therefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fB as the best overall match for the role."}
